From 825fa89ca4dd1eae334a542f5368d19b1347ea9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ohos-kernel-port contributors <232252@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:44:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix the build errors in the 6.6 tree
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Baseline: gitcode.com/openharmony/kernel_linux_6.6
Branch:   OpenHarmony-7.0-Release
Commit:   f4b61510491aa20f7f57fbbc5efc754083c92212

Reported by a full arm64 build of lane ohos-7.0-6.6:

  kernel/sched/rtg/rtg_ctrl.c:430:19: error: function declaration isn't a
      prototype [-Werror=strict-prototypes]
  mm/zswapd_control.c:848:29: error: 'eswap_info_show' undeclared here
  drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf-process-info.c:34:12: error: 'struct dma_buf' has no
      member named 'exp_pid'  (and 'exp_task_comm', 12 times in that file)

1.  rtg_ctrl.c has one definition with an empty parameter list.  In C, f()
    declares unspecified arguments rather than none, and the kernel builds with
    -Werror=strict-prototypes.  Only the definition at line 430 is changed; the
    three call sites at 447, 512 and 540 are left as they are.  An earlier
    revision of this patch rewrote those too, which produced "too many
    arguments to function 'curr_grp_id'".

2.  eswap_info_show is defined inside #ifdef CONFIG_HYPERHOLD_DEBUG but its
    cftype entry is not, so with that option off — what
    kernel_linux_config's type/standard_defconfig gives — the handler is
    referenced with no declaration.  The entry now carries the same guard as
    the zswapd_vmstat_show entry above it, which is the pattern this file
    already uses for a debug-only proc file.

3.  include/linux/dma-buf.h has no CONFIG_DMABUF_PROCESS_INFO block at all,
    yet drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf-process-info.c in this same tree uses exp_pid
    and exp_task_comm twelve times.  The two fields are added under the guard
    the 5.10 tree uses for them, so the 6.6 struct matches 5.10's and the
    driver compiles.  They are inert unless the option is set.

Note: this tree's drivers/accesstokenid/access_tokenid.c already spells its
function with (void); an earlier revision of this patch was generated with a
blanket substitution that "fixed" the call sites there too and broke the build
in a new way.

Upstream: no equivalent; these are OpenHarmony additions, and the 6.6 tree's
struct dma_buf and its own dma-buf-process-info.c disagree with each other.
Licence: GPL-2.0-only, same as the tree.
---
 include/linux/dma-buf.h     | 4 ++++
 kernel/sched/rtg/rtg_ctrl.c | 2 +-
 mm/zswapd_control.c         | 2 ++
 3 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/dma-buf.h b/include/linux/dma-buf.h
index 3f31baa..e02d5fa 100644
--- a/include/linux/dma-buf.h
+++ b/include/linux/dma-buf.h
@@ -422,6 +422,10 @@ struct dma_buf {
 	 * obeying fences. See enum dma_resv_usage for further descriptions.
 	 */
 	struct dma_resv *resv;
+#ifdef CONFIG_DMABUF_PROCESS_INFO
+	pid_t exp_pid;
+	char exp_task_comm[TASK_COMM_LEN];
+#endif
 
 	/** @poll: for userspace poll support */
 	wait_queue_head_t poll;
diff --git a/kernel/sched/rtg/rtg_ctrl.c b/kernel/sched/rtg/rtg_ctrl.c
index 164f1b2..0cab1f8 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/rtg/rtg_ctrl.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/rtg/rtg_ctrl.c
@@ -427,7 +427,7 @@ int update_frame_state(int grp_id, int margin, bool in_frame)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-static inline int curr_grp_id()
+static inline int curr_grp_id(void)
 {
 	return sched_get_group_id(current);
 }
diff --git a/mm/zswapd_control.c b/mm/zswapd_control.c
index 80f7bc3..f6fd0c5 100644
--- a/mm/zswapd_control.c
+++ b/mm/zswapd_control.c
@@ -842,11 +842,13 @@ static struct cftype zswapd_policy_files[] = {
 		.seq_show = zswapd_vmstat_show,
 	},
 #endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_HYPERHOLD_DEBUG
 	{
 		.name = "eswap_info",
 		.flags = CFTYPE_ONLY_ON_ROOT,
 		.seq_show = eswap_info_show,
 	},
+#endif
 
 	{ },	/* terminate */
 };
-- 
2.39.5

